// EXTRACTION NOTE. The supplied markdown is a flattened conversion that
// interleaves the book's two columns, so one skill's upgrades can land under
// another skill's name. These entries were rebuilt from the PDF instead, with
// reading order reconstructed from block geometry, then cross-checked against
// the markdown: 104 of 113 names matched outright, and every difference was
// explained — 7 were markdown corruption the PDF gets right (Character Actor,
// Hide in Shadows, Wrasslin', ...), and 2 were skills the markdown pass had
// silently dropped because they carry a flavour tagline between the name and
// the keyword line (Pugilism, Noggin Nocker).
//
// Mechanics only: no flavour text. The app needs the numbers, and the rules
// prose belongs to the people who wrote it.
//
// checkType: 'evade' (all Attack Skills roll against the target's Evade),
// 'passive' (never rolled), 'opposed' or 'unopposed' for Utility Skills.

